WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.340
Six phases.

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:03.659
Three hundred and forty emails tracked.

00:00:03.659 --> 00:00:07.863
One hundred and thirteen clean MPs with an accountability score of zero.

00:00:07.863 --> 00:00:10.147
Nine priority targets identified.

00:00:10.147 --> 00:00:14.602
This is the political accountability campaign — and every phase is documented.

00:00:14.602 --> 00:00:16.147
Phase One — Seed.

00:00:16.147 --> 00:00:22.409
Four media targets: CJPME, the Western Standard, Read the Maple, and Esprit de Corps.

00:00:22.409 --> 00:00:25.272
Get the story into outlets that will actually publish it.

00:00:25.272 --> 00:00:27.022
Phase Two — Recruit.

00:00:27.022 --> 00:00:31.681
Nine priority MPs plus one hundred and thirteen clean MPs across all parties.

00:00:31.681 --> 00:00:33.159
Cross-party alignment.

00:00:33.159 --> 00:00:34.590
This is not partisan.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:38.340
Phase Three — Arm. Party-specific accountability preparation.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.999
Phase Four — Pressure.

00:00:39.999 --> 00:00:45.727
Trigger committee studies at ETHI — the Ethics Committee — and NDDN — the National Defence Committee.

00:00:45.727 --> 00:00:48.613
Force the evidence onto the parliamentary record.

00:00:48.613 --> 00:00:50.318
Phase Five — Trap.

00:00:50.318 --> 00:00:52.499
Five Private Members' Bills queued.

00:00:52.499 --> 00:00:54.068
Legislation drafted.

00:00:54.068 --> 00:00:55.218
Ready to file.

00:00:55.218 --> 00:00:56.999
Phase Six — Close.

00:00:56.999 --> 00:00:58.931
Five-wall strategic closure.

00:00:58.931 --> 00:01:00.011
Parliamentary.

00:01:00.011 --> 00:01:00.829
Legal.

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:01.590
Media.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:02.420
Public.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.545
International.

00:01:03.545 --> 00:01:04.920
Every exit blocked.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.022
Every escape route documented.

00:01:07.022 --> 00:01:10.227
Three Bloc Québécois kingmakers hold the balance of power.

00:01:10.227 --> 00:01:14.352
Yves-François Blanchet, Claude Thériault, and Kristina Michaud.

00:01:14.352 --> 00:01:17.806
In a minority parliament, three votes can bring down a government.

00:01:17.806 --> 00:01:20.022
This campaign knows where those votes are.
